---
// Every statement here was checked against the live site and the code on
// 2026-09-29: the host's injected script and its cookies, no analytics, no
// error tracking, what the feedback form keeps. These change it, so update
// this page with them: turning on analytics (PUBLIC_CF_ANALYTICS_TOKEN, see
// BaseLayout) or error tracking (SENTRY_DSN, see astro.config.mjs), changing
// what public/feedback.php keeps, or adding anything that loads from another
// site.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What Learn Civic Sense collects, what its host and image service see, and what the feedback form keeps."
  width="narrow"
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">What happens to your data when you use this site, in plain words.</p>

    <h2>What this site collects</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing about you while you read. There are no accounts or logins, no analytics, no
      advertising and no error tracking, and the site sets no cookies of its own.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your theme choice.</strong> If you pick Light or Dark in the theme menu, the choice is
        kept in your own browser (local storage) so the next page uses it. It never leaves your device.
        With System, nothing is kept.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Search</strong> runs in your browser: the site sends it parts of a search index, and what
        you type is not sent as text to us or to anyone else.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="feedback">The feedback form</h2>
    <p>
      If you send feedback, the site receives what you chose it is about and your message (up to 500
      characters). It is emailed to the person who runs this site and is not stored on the website.
      The form doesn’t ask for your name or email address, so there is no way to reply to you;
      please leave personal details out of the message.
    </p>
    <p>
      So that no one can flood the form, the server keeps, for each sender, a keyed hash of their IP
      address (a code worked out from it, not the address itself) with the times they sent feedback.
      Entries older than a day are no longer used, and are deleted the next time anyone uses the
      form.
    </p>

    <h2>What others see</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Our host, GoDaddy,</strong> runs the web server. Like any web server, it receives your
        IP address and the addresses of the pages you open.
        <a href="https://www.godaddy.com/legal/agreements/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >GoDaddy’s privacy notice</a
        > covers what it keeps.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>GoDaddy also adds its own script to every page</strong>, for monitoring performance
        (loaded from img1.wsimg.com). That script sets three cookies (<code>_tccl_visitor</code>,
        <code>_tccl_visit</code> and <code>_scc_session</code>) and sends its measurements to
        GoDaddy (secureserver.net). We did not add it; its own note says opting out goes through
        GoDaddy’s hosting support.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Lesson illustrations</strong> come from ImageKit (ik.imagekit.io), an image service. Your
        browser loads them from ImageKit, which sees your IP address as any site serving an image does.
        See
        <a href="https://imagekit.io/privacy-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >ImageKit’s privacy policy</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Share buttons</strong> are plain links. Nothing from WhatsApp, X, LinkedIn or Telegram
        loads on this site; they are involved only when you tap one.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      Every lesson can be read with cookies and scripts blocked. Search, the quiz and the theme menu
      need JavaScript, but none of them needs a cookie. A content blocker such as
      <a href="https://privacybadger.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Privacy Badger</a> stops the host’s
      script.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions, use the <a href="/feedback/">feedback form</a> (choose “Report something”)
      or open an issue on
      <a href="https://github.com/gragtajar/lcs/issues" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >our GitHub repository</a
      >.
    </p>

    <p class="meta">Last updated: 2026-09-29.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-2);
  }
  .legal .lede {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
  .legal p,
  .legal ul {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .legal ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
  }
  .legal li {
    margin-block: var(--space-2);
  }
  .legal code {
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
  .legal .meta {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }
</style>
